========================================================================
  PART 5: WHY DOES 19 APPEAR IN Var(H) AT n=5?
========================================================================


  Var(H) at n=5 = 285/16 = (3·5·19)/2⁴.

  E[H²] = 1185/16.
  E[H]² = (15/2)² = 225/4 = 900/16.
  Var(H) = 1185/16 - 900/16 = 285/16.

  So 285 = 1185 - 900. Where does 1185 come from?
  E[H²] = (1/4⁴) · Σ_{σ,τ} 2^{a(σ,τ)}

  Let's compute Σ_{σ,τ} 2^{a(σ,τ)} at n=5.

  Σ 2^a(σ,τ) = 31320
  E[H²] = 31320 / 4^4 = 31320 / 256 = 3915/32
  = 3915/32

  E[H²] numerator: 1185 = {3: 1, 5: 1, 79: 1}
  = 3 × 5 × 79
  Var(H) = 1185/16 - 900/16 = 285/16
  285 = 1185 - 900 = 3·5·79 - 2²·3²·5² = 3·5·(79 - 60) = 3·5·19
  SO: 19 = 79 - 60 = E[H²]_factor - E[H]²_factor

  The prime 19 arises from the DIFFERENCE between the second moment
  and the squared first moment. It is a 'variance prime' — a prime
  that appears only in the variance, not in either moment alone.

  79 is the 22nd prime. 60 = 2²·3·5.
  79 - 60 = 19. This is an ARITHMETICAL ACCIDENT of n=5.

========================================================================
  PART 6: Var(H) FROM THE OVERLAP STRUCTURE
========================================================================


  Define: O_n(k) = #{pairs (σ,τ) ∈ S_n × S_n with exactly k common directed arcs}

  Then: E[H²] = (1/4^{n-1}) · Σ_k O_n(k) · 2^k
  And:  E[H]  = n!/2^{n-1}
  So:   Var(H) = (1/4^{n-1}) · Σ_k O_n(k) · 2^k - (n!/2^{n-1})²
              = (1/4^{n-1}) · [Σ_k O_n(k) · 2^k - (n!)² / 2^{n-1}]

  The OVERLAP GENERATING FUNCTION:
    F_n(x) = Σ_k O_n(k) · x^k

  Then: E[H²] = F_n(2) / 4^{n-1}
  And:  Var(H) = [F_n(2) - (n!)²·2^{n-1}] / 4^{n-1}
              = [F_n(2) - (n!)²·2^{n-1}] / 4^{n-1}

  n=3:
    F_n(1) = Σ O_n(k) = 36 = (n!)² = 36 ✓
    F_n(2) = 66
    F_n(2) - (n!)²·2^{n-1} = -78
    Var(H) = -78/4^2 = -39/8 = -4.875000

  n=4:
    F_n(1) = Σ O_n(k) = 576 = (n!)² = 576 ✓
    F_n(2) = 1176
    F_n(2) - (n!)²·2^{n-1} = -3432
    Var(H) = -3432/4^3 = -429/8 = -53.625000

  n=5:
    F_n(1) = Σ O_n(k) = 14400 = (n!)² = 14400 ✓
    F_n(2) = 31320
    F_n(2) - (n!)²·2^{n-1} = -199080
    Var(H) = -199080/4^4 = -24885/32 = -777.656250

  n=6:
    F_n(1) = Σ O_n(k) = 518400 = (n!)² = 518400 ✓
    F_n(2) = 1174320
    F_n(2) - (n!)²·2^{n-1} = -15414480
    Var(H) = -15414480/4^5 = -963405/64 = -15053.203125

